.TH WMNM-ASKPASS 1 "September 2025" "wmnm" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wmnm-askpass \- ask for a password in a WINGs dialog
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wmnm-askpass
.RI [ prompt ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wmnm-askpass
displays a dialog with a masked text field, writes what was typed to standard
output, and exits zero.  If the user cancels, nothing is written and the exit
status is non-zero.
.PP
The dialog is built with WINGs, Window Maker's own widget set, so it matches
the rest of a Window Maker desktop and needs no other toolkit.
.PP
This is the convention used by
.BR ssh (1),
.BR git (1)
and
.BR sudo (8),
so although
.B wmnm-askpass
exists for
.BR wmnm (1),
it works as a general purpose askpass program.
.SH EXAMPLES
Use it for ssh keys:
.PP
.RS
.nf
SSH_ASKPASS=wmnm-askpass SSH_ASKPASS_REQUIRE=prefer ssh-add
.fi
.RE
.PP
For git over HTTPS:
.PP
.RS
.nf
git config --global core.askPass wmnm-askpass
.fi
.RE
.PP
For sudo:
.PP
.RS
.nf
SUDO_ASKPASS=/usr/bin/wmnm-askpass sudo -A command
.fi
.RE
.PP
To make it the system default on Debian and derivatives:
.PP
.RS
.nf
update-alternatives --install /usr/bin/ssh-askpass ssh-askpass \\
    /usr/bin/wmnm-askpass 50
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
A password was entered and written to standard output.
.TP
.B 1
The user cancelled, or the display could not be opened.
.SH NOTES
.BR pinentry (1)
is not interchangeable with this program.  It speaks the Assuan protocol on
standard input and output rather than taking a prompt as an argument, so
.B wmnm-askpass
cannot be used as a pinentry and pinentry cannot be used as an askpass.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wmnm (1),
.BR ssh-add (1),
.BR sudo (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Doug Torrance <dtorrance@piedmont.edu>
